id: pmc-n4qu
title: Refuse explicit partial-read envelopes supplied to changelog generation
description: "Implement https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/issues/224 using the public SDK completeness validator while preserving intentional bare-array subsets and status/date selection."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: correctness,regression,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-07T12:47:52.397Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T15:54:22.369Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T12:48:39.040Z",codex-sol,"Built-package reproduction of #224: paginated and row-compacted stdin returned exit 0 and replaced retained full history with one item. Plan: refuse explicit unsafe envelope receipts with the public SDK inspector; preserve receipt-free subsets and ordinary status/date filters. The SDK certificate targets a stricter whole unfiltered workspace contract, so caller-selected scope needs an adapter rather than certification as the whole workspace."
  "2026-10-07T12:53:38.818Z",codex-sol,"Regression suite passes 52/52, including complete filtered inputs and receipt-free subsets. Function-only behavioural revert restored just parsePmItemsJson to the base implementation, kept tests and imports intact, and rebuilt the package: 48 receipt assertions and file/stdin nonzero-exit assertions failed as expected; positive controls passed. Restored the fix and rebuilt. SDK limitation: inspectCompleteListResult has only a whole-unfiltered-workspace policy, so the caller-input adapter supplies defaults for absent legacy proofs and ignores scope filters without issuing a completeness certificate."
  "2026-10-07T12:54:47.531Z",codex-sol,"The peer minimum is now the tested SDK 2026.10.4, ensuring the new static public inspector import exists instead of leaving older peer versions advertised as supported. Linked regression run passed 52/52 under pm test as well as direct execution. Release coverage is running at the unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-07T12:56:05.590Z",codex-sol,"npm run release:check passed: 585 tests, zero failures/skips, configured 100% lines/branches/functions across all 12 required source files, docstrings, production audit, pack dry run, changelog consistency, release date and publish-attestation checks. bun run release:check is next. The PM-linked regression command passed 52/52 with no SDK mocks."
  "2026-10-07T12:58:22.492Z",codex-sol,The first Bun gate caught an inconsistent extension manifest floor after the new SDK peer minimum was introduced. Aligned manifest.json pm_min_version and its real SDK host compatibility regression with 2026.10.4. No runtime implementation changed; final npm and Bun gates will be rerun after this correction.
  "2026-10-07T13:00:36.658Z",codex-sol,"Corrected bun run release:check passed: 585/585 tests, zero skips, 100% configured lines/branches/functions, and all release checks. Original #224 built-package input now exits 1 with page_incomplete, count_mismatch, read_output_invalid and budget_compaction findings, count=1 of total=2, empty stdout, and byte-identical retained full history. README and usage docs explain the refusal and caller-owned subset path. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator closure; final commit will be checked with both release commands before pushing."
  "2026-10-07T15:54:22.369Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeRabbit 4208662777 (valid, Major): a caller envelope could carry complete_list: false (or a contradicted certificate) and still replace the changelog, because inspectCompleteListResult ignores the field and certifyCompleteListResult re-issues certificates rather than reading one. A supplied certificate must now deep-equal the certificate the SDK issues for the delivered rows and receipts (caller status/date scope normalized as for inspection); uncertifiable receipts refuse. Tests: negative, denied-source, contradicted-count and receipt-stripped forged certificates; parse-level tests fail on revert."
files[6]{path,scope}:
  manifest.json,project
  package-lock.json,project
  package.json,project
  src/generator.ts,project
  test/extension.test.ts,project
  test/input-completeness.test.ts,project
tests[3]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
